<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Council of Aragon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1494">1494</a>–<a href="/years/1707">1707</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-aragon">Aragon</a> was the royal council that advised the Spanish monarchs on the government of the Crown of Aragon, comprising Aragon, Catalonia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balearic-islands">Balearic Islands</a>. Created by Ferdinand II in 1494, it sat at the royal court and handled appointments, justice and petitions for kingdoms whose rulers rarely visited them. Philip V abolished it in 1707 after suppressing the separate Aragonese laws during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After the union with Castile, the <b>Council of Aragon</b>, created by Ferdinand II in 1494, advised the absent king on the affairs of his eastern realms.</blockquote><a href="/empire/crown-of-aragon">Crown of Aragon · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>…the polysynodal regime: the Councils of State and War for foreign policy, the Council of Castile for justice and internal government, the <b>Councils of Aragon</b>, Italy, Portugal and Flanders for those territories, the Council of the Indies, founded in 1524, for the Americas, and the Council of Finance.</blockquote><a href="/empire/habsburg-spain">Habsburg Spain · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>In October 1936 the CNT created the Regional Defence <b>Council of Aragon</b>, first at Fraga and then at Caspe, under Joaquín Ascaso.</blockquote><a href="/state/regional-defence-council-of-aragon">Regional Defence Council of Aragon</a></li></ul></section>
